This appears to be a CBP ruling on a VR controller. Hand-held radio remote controls for VR headsets are generally classified in 8526.92 (radio remote control apparatus), and the statistical suffix is 8526.92.5000 ("Other" radio remote control apparatus). Other candidates include 8537.10 and 8543.70, but the description stresses "radio remote controller" using RF, which points to 8526.92.

The HTSUS breakdown is 8526.92.10 for radio remote control apparatus used for civil aircraft, and 8526.92.50 for other. The 10-digit statistical form is 8526.92.5000.

{"hts_code": "8526.92.5000", "reason": "A hand-held RF wireless controller that remotely controls applications on a VR headset is radio remote control apparatus under heading 8526, subheading 8526.92 (other than for civil aircraft)."}
